---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="The Organization" description="Mathim Divisions began as an imaginary organization for everything. The name endured; the work became real.">
  <section class="interior-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow"><span class="signal"></span>About / The organization</p>
      <h1>A name for<br /><em>what comes next.</em></h1>
      <p>There was never any requirement that the work belong to one field. The name came first. The disciplines followed.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="editorial-section">
    <div class="container editorial-columns">
      <p class="editorial-kicker">01 / Mandate</p>
      <div class="editorial-copy">
        <h2>Built to contain<br />the unexpected.</h2>
        <p>Mathim Divisions is an independent umbrella for technical projects, creative endeavors, writing, and research. It gives unlike things a shared home without insisting that they become alike.</p>
        <p>Some work is practical and immediate: understanding systems, making documentation, and building tools. Some is exploratory: experiments in intelligence and computation, essays, and ideas that may not yet have a category.</p>
        <p>The divisions are descriptions of work, not borders around it.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="editorial-section alt">
    <div class="container editorial-columns">
      <p class="editorial-kicker">02 / Provenance</p>
      <div class="editorial-copy">
        <h2>The name<br />predates the work.</h2>
        <p>Long before it appeared on a real website, Mathim Divisions was a fictional company invented by two friends, Cassie and Cameron. It could make a product, operate a business, or be the organization behind whatever they imagined next.</p>
        <p>Years later, with Cameron's blessing, Cassie kept the name. The concept has changed surprisingly little: an open-ended place for things worth making.</p>
        <p class="note">An organization of organizations, at least in spirit. No fictional headcount, financial results, or clients required.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="editorial-section">
    <div class="container editorial-columns">
      <p class="editorial-kicker">03 / Present operations</p>
      <div class="editorial-copy">
        <h2>Small by choice.<br />Wide by nature.</h2>
        <p>Current work spans independent AI research, technical practice, writing, and digital tools. The Smol Model Company of New Haven is an affiliated research initiative focused on useful intelligence under real-world constraints.</p>
        <div class="index-table">
          <div class="index-line"><span class="index">01</span><div><h3>The Smol Model Company</h3><p>Independent experimental AI research.</p></div><a href="https://thesmolmodel.co" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Visit ↗</a></div>
          <div class="index-line"><span class="index">02</span><div><h3>Technical practice</h3><p>Systems, documentation, and tools.</p></div><a href="/services#systems">Explore ↗</a></div>
          <div class="index-line"><span class="index">03</span><div><h3>Writing & creative work</h3><p>Publications, experiments, and a home for what comes next.</p></div><a href="/services#publications">Explore ↗</a></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>